* Genuine Georgia Tech XSPICE d_dlatch original digital code model.
* Original 1991 ifspec port order: DATA ENABLE SET RESET Q NQ, type d.
* Each original digital input is promoted to state/sink/source for our
* physical ALB load ABI, and Q/NQ are exported as independent analog pins
* through the stock ngspice dac_bridge. The latch semantics remain STOCK.
.subckt SR_GT_DLATCH DATA DATA_SINK DATA_SOURCE EN EN_SINK EN_SOURCE SET SET_SINK SET_SOURCE RESET RESET_SINK RESET_SOURCE OUT NOUT
Adata_load DATA DATA_SINK DATA_SOURCE INPUT_LOAD
Aenable_load EN EN_SINK EN_SOURCE INPUT_LOAD
Aset_load SET SET_SINK SET_SOURCE INPUT_LOAD
Areset_load RESET RESET_SINK RESET_SOURCE INPUT_LOAD
.model INPUT_LOAD sr_bundle_load(capacitance=2p sink_current=0 source_current=0)
Alatch DATA EN SET RESET Q NQ GT_ORIGINAL_LATCH
.model GT_ORIGINAL_LATCH d_dlatch(data_delay=400p enable_delay=900p set_delay=500p reset_delay=650p ic=0 rise_delay=100p fall_delay=200p data_load=0 enable_load=0 set_load=0 reset_load=0)
Aout [Q NQ] [OUT NOUT] GT_ORIGINAL_DAC
.model GT_ORIGINAL_DAC dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high=3.3 out_undef=1.65 input_load=0 t_rise=50p t_fall=50p)
.ends SR_GT_DLATCH
